Even the ordinary ones can turn invisible, destroy your armour, drain your
strength (by 1d5 points or more), and curse your stuff (and with neither
magic resistance nor half spell damage, that's 1d6 items).
Additionally, they are absolutely guaranteed to be generated hostile,
and are immune to death rays and sleep effects.

Golden nagas crop up at a similar sort of depth, and have similar
capabilities, and move faster, but are susceptible to death rays and
sleep effects, and are not guaranteed to be hostile.

Finally: A monster doesn't have to kill you to be responsible for your
death.
